---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;

const lastUpdated = '2026-05-15';
---

<Layout title="Sources & Citations | Waseem's SEO Guide">
  <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <ol>
      <li><a href={`${base}/`}>Home</a></li>
      <li aria-current="page">Sources &amp; Citations</li>
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <header>
    <span class="badge">📚 REFERENCES</span>
    <h1>Sources &amp; Citations</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">Every factual claim in this course traces back to a primary source. Verify, challenge, learn deeper.</p>
    <div class="reading-time-badge">⏱️ Reference page — bookmark it</div>
    <div class="meta">
      <strong>Last verified:</strong> {lastUpdated}<br />
      <strong>Method:</strong> Direct links to original publishers (Google Search Central, web.dev, schema.org, peer-reviewed papers, industry research).
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="intro">
    <div class="highlight-box">
      <h4>Why a sources page?</h4>
      <p>Most SEO courses make claims like "use INP under 200ms" without telling you <em>where</em> that number comes from. That's the same fluffy, unsourced content that AI search now demotes. This page is the antidote — and a model for what your own content should look like.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Primary Sources -->
  <section id="primary">
    <h2>🏛️ Primary Sources (Google, W3C, web.dev)</h2>
    <p>These are publications from the platforms themselves. They override any third-party interpretation.</p>

    <h3>Google Search Central</h3>
    <ul class="sources-list">
      <li>
        <a href="https://developers.google.com/search" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Search Central — main documentation</a>
        <p>The single most authoritative source on what Google's crawler and ranking systems do. Updated continuously.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://developers.google.com/search/blog" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Search Central Blog</a>
        <p>Where algorithm updates, deprecations, and new ranking signals are first announced.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://services.google.com/fh/files/misc/hsw-sqrg.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Search Quality Rater Guidelines (PDF, official)</a>
        <p>The actual rubric Google's 16,000+ quality raters use. Defines E-E-A-T, "Lowest quality" pages, and YMYL ("Your Money or Your Life") topics.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://developers.google.com/search/docs/essentials/spam-policies" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Spam Policies</a>
        <p>What Google considers spam: link schemes, cloaking, doorway pages, scaled content abuse, expired domain abuse, etc.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://developers.google.com/search/docs/appearance/structured-data/search-gallery" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Rich Results / Structured Data Gallery</a>
        <p>Every Schema type Google currently supports for rich results (FAQ, HowTo, Recipe, Product, etc.).</p>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>web.dev (Google's developer publication)</h3>
    <ul class="sources-list">
      <li>
        <a href="https://web.dev/blog/inp-cwv-march-12" target="_blank" rel="noopener">"INP becomes a Core Web Vital" (March 12, 2024)</a>
        <p>The official announcement replacing FID with INP. <strong>Cited in:</strong> Level 2, Level 3 final test.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://web.dev/articles/inp" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Interaction to Next Paint (INP) — definition &amp; thresholds</a>
        <p>Good ≤200ms, Poor &gt;500ms. The numbers you must memorize.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://web.dev/articles/optimize-inp" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Optimize INP — concrete techniques</a>
        <p>Long-task breakdown, scheduler.yield, content-visibility, isInputPending. Source for the optimization tips in Level 2.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://web.dev/articles/lcp" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Largest Contentful Paint (LCP)</a>
        <p>Good ≤2.5s, Poor &gt;4s. What "largest contentful element" means.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://web.dev/articles/cls" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS)</a>
        <p>Good ≤0.1, Poor &gt;0.25. How layout shift scores are calculated.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://web.dev/explore/learn-core-web-vitals" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Learn Core Web Vitals — course track</a>
        <p>Free, in-depth CWV training direct from the Chrome team.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>E-E-A-T &amp; Quality Updates</h3>
    <ul class="sources-list">
      <li>
        <a href="https://developers.google.com/search/blog/2022/12/google-raters-guidelines-e-e-a-t" target="_blank" rel="noopener">"Our latest update to the quality rater guidelines: E-E-A-T" (Dec 15, 2022)</a>
        <p>When Google added the second "E" for Experience. <strong>Cited in:</strong> Level 3 E-E-A-T section.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://developers.google.com/search/blog/2022/08/helpful-content-update" target="_blank" rel="noopener">"Helpful Content Update" (August 2022)</a>
        <p>The algorithm change that began demoting "content written for search engines, not people."</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://blog.google/products/search/generative-ai-google-search-may-2024/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">"AI Overviews and more" (May 14, 2024)</a>
        <p>Official rollout of AI Overviews to US Search. <strong>Cited in:</strong> Level 3 AI Overviews section.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>schema.org &amp; W3C</h3>
    <ul class="sources-list">
      <li>
        <a href="https://schema.org/docs/full.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">schema.org — full type hierarchy</a>
        <p>Authoritative definitions for every Schema type and property.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://json-ld.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">JSON-LD 1.1 specification</a>
        <p>The W3C spec for the format Google now prefers for structured data.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://www.sitemaps.org/protocol.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">sitemaps.org — protocol</a>
        <p>The XML sitemap specification all major search engines follow.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Other primary docs</h3>
    <ul class="sources-list">
      <li>
        <a href="https://llmstxt.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">llmstxt.org — the llms.txt proposal</a>
        <p>Jeremy Howard (Answer.AI), 2024. The proposed standard for telling LLM agents the curated entry points to your site. <strong>Cited in:</strong> Level 3 llms.txt section.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robots.txt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">robots.txt (RFC 9309)</a>
        <p>Standardized in 2022 as IETF RFC 9309.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- Research & Studies -->
  <section id="research">
    <h2>🔬 Peer-Reviewed Research &amp; Industry Studies</h2>
    <p>When primary docs don't cover a topic, defer to well-designed third-party research with disclosed methodology.</p>

    <ul class="sources-list">
      <li>
        <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.09735" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Aggarwal et al., 2023 — "GEO: Generative Engine Optimization"</a>
        <p>The original academic paper coining "GEO." Princeton + Georgia Tech + Allen AI. Quantifies which content features get cited in AI-generated answers (~30% visibility lift from citations + statistics). <strong>Cited in:</strong> Level 3 AI Overviews section.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://ahrefs.com/blog/seo-statistics/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ahrefs — SEO Statistics (continuously updated)</a>
        <p>Largest public dataset of organic search analyses. Worth bookmarking for CTR-by-position, % of pages with zero traffic, etc.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://ahrefs.com/blog/how-long-does-it-take-to-rank/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ahrefs — "How long does it take to rank?" study</a>
        <p>Analysis of 2M+ pages: only 5.7% rank in top 10 within 1 year. Reality check for content marketers.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://backlinko.com/google-ranking-factors" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Backlinko — Google ranking factors (annual update)</a>
        <p>Brian Dean's data-driven analysis. Strong on backlink correlations.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://sparktoro.com/blog/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SparkToro Research Blog (Rand Fishkin)</a>
        <p>Zero-click search studies. Very influential for understanding SERP-without-click realities.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://www.semrush.com/research/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Semrush Research</a>
        <p>"State of Search" reports, AI search analyses, BrightEdge studies.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- AI &amp; LLM Sources -->
  <section id="ai-sources">
    <h2>🤖 AI / GEO Sources</h2>

    <ul class="sources-list">
      <li>
        <a href="https://openai.com/policies/bot/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenAI — GPTBot crawler docs</a>
        <p>What GPTBot indexes, how to opt out via robots.txt.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://docs.perplexity.ai/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Perplexity Docs</a>
        <p>How Perplexity searches and cites sources.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Anthropic (Claude)</a>
        <p>Maker of Claude. Claude with web tools cites sources visibly.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://blog.google/products/search/ai-mode-search/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google — AI Mode in Search</a>
        <p>The successor to SGE.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- Industry Publications -->
  <section id="industry">
    <h2>📰 Trustworthy Industry Publications</h2>
    <p>For ongoing algorithm-update news, these are the publications working SEOs actually read.</p>

    <ul class="sources-list">
      <li>
        <a href="https://searchengineland.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Search Engine Land</a>
        <p>Owned by Third Door Media. Best for breaking news on Google updates. Use as a first read; verify with primary sources.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://www.searchenginejournal.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Search Engine Journal</a>
        <p>How-to-focused, contributor-driven. Quality varies by author — check the author bio.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://moz.com/blog" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Moz Blog &amp; Whiteboard Friday</a>
        <p>Long-running educational resource. The "Beginner's Guide to SEO" is a classic.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://www.aleydasolis.com/en/learning-seo/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Learning SEO — Aleyda Solís</a>
        <p>Curated, free SEO learning roadmap from one of the most respected technical SEOs.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://www.searchenginewatch.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Search Engine Watch</a>
        <p>One of the oldest SEO publications. Trend and analysis pieces.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- Tools -->
  <section id="tools">
    <h2>🛠️ Tools Referenced in This Course</h2>

    <h3>Free</h3>
    <ul class="sources-list">
      <li><a href="https://search.google.com/search-console" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Search Console</a> — your free SEO dashboard, direct from Google.</li>
      <li><a href="https://pagespeed.web.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PageSpeed Insights</a> — official CWV testing.</li>
      <li><a href="https://search.google.com/test/rich-results" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Rich Results Test</a> — Schema validator (Google).</li>
      <li><a href="https://validator.schema.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Schema Markup Validator</a> — generic JSON-LD/microdata validator.</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.google.com/business/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Business Profile</a> — free local listing.</li>
      <li><a href="https://developer.chrome.com/docs/lighthouse/overview/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Chrome Lighthouse</a> — built-in audit tool (F12 → Lighthouse).</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.bing.com/webmasters/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Bing Webmaster Tools</a> — same for Bing (powers ChatGPT Search).</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.opengraph.xyz" target="_blank" rel="noopener">opengraph.xyz</a> — preview Open Graph cards across platforms.</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.ssllabs.com/ssltest/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SSL Labs</a> — test your HTTPS implementation.</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.connectively.us" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Connectively (formerly HARO)</a> — journalist requests for expert quotes.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Freemium</h3>
    <ul class="sources-list">
      <li><a href="https://ahrefs.com/webmaster-tools" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ahrefs Webmaster Tools (free)</a> — backlinks &amp; site audit for your verified domains.</li>
      <li><a href="https://neilpatel.com/ubersuggest/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ubersuggest</a> — limited free keyword + competitor analysis.</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.semrush.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Semrush</a> — paid, but 14-day free trial covers a real audit.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="closing">
    <div class="success-box">
      <h4>📝 How to use this page</h4>
      <ol>
        <li>Bookmark this page. SEO changes fast; primary sources update first.</li>
        <li>When you read a claim in this course, click through to verify the source. Don't trust the course author — trust the original.</li>
        <li>Build your own "sources page" for your niche. It's one of the strongest E-E-A-T signals you can ship.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <nav class="level-nav">
    <a href={`${base}/`} class="nav-btn">🏠 Back to Home</a>
    <a href={`${base}/glossary`} class="nav-btn">📖 Glossary →</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .breadcrumbs { margin-bottom: 30px; }
  .breadcrumbs ol { display: flex; list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .breadcrumbs li { color: var(--color-text-muted); }
  .breadcrumbs li:not(:last-child)::after { content: '→'; margin-left: 8px; color: var(--color-text-muted); }
  .breadcrumbs a { color: var(--color-link); text-decoration: none; }
  .breadcrumbs a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

  header { text-align: center; margin-bottom: 40px; }
  .badge {
    display: inline-block;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #667eea 0%, #764ba2 100%);
    color: white;
    padding: 8px 20px;
    border-radius: 25px;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  header h1 { font-size: 2.5em; margin-bottom: 10px; color: var(--color-text); }
  .subtitle { font-size: 1.2em; color: var(--color-brand-primary); margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .reading-time-badge { display: inline-block; background: var(--color-surface-elevated); padding: 6px 16px; border-radius: 15px; font-size: 0.9em; color: var(--color-text-muted); }
  .meta { margin-top: 20px; color: var(--color-text-muted); line-height: 1.8; }

  section { margin-bottom: 50px; }
  section h2 { color: var(--color-text); margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 1.8em; padding-bottom: 10px; border-bottom: 3px solid var(--color-brand-primary); }
  section h3 { color: var(--color-brand-primary); margin: 25px 0 15px; font-size: 1.3em; }

  .sources-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 15px;
  }
  .sources-list li {
    background: var(--color-surface-elevated);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-brand-primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 15px 20px;
    transition: transform 0.2s ease, box-shadow 0.2s ease;
  }
  .sources-list li:hover { transform: translateX(4px); box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm); }
  .sources-list a { color: var(--color-link); text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.05em; }
  .sources-list a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .sources-list p { margin: 6px 0 0; color: var(--color-text-secondary); font-size: 0.95em; line-height: 1.6; }

  .highlight-box {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #fff3cd 0%, #ffeaa7 100%);
    border-left: 5px solid var(--color-warning);
    padding: 20px;
    border-radius: 12px;
    margin: 20px 0;
  }
  .highlight-box h4 { margin: 0 0 10px; color: #856404; }

  .success-box {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #d4edda 0%, #c3e6cb 100%);
    border-left: 5px solid var(--color-success);
    padding: 20px;
    border-radius: 12px;
    margin: 20px 0;
  }
  .success-box h4 { margin: 0 0 10px; color: #155724; }
  .success-box ol { margin: 10px 0 0 20px; color: #155724; }

  .level-nav {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 20px;
    margin-top: 50px;
    padding-top: 30px;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--color-border-light);
  }
  .level-nav .nav-btn {
    padding: 12px 24px;
    background: var(--color-brand-gradient);
    color: white;
    text-decoration: none;
    border-radius: 12px;
    font-weight: 500;
    transition: all 0.3s;
  }
  .level-nav .nav-btn:hover { transform: translateY(-2px); box-shadow: var(--shadow-md); }

  :global([data-theme="dark"]) .highlight-box {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #3a3a2a 0%, #4a4a3a 100%);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }
  :global([data-theme="dark"]) .highlight-box h4 { color: var(--color-warning); }
  :global([data-theme="dark"]) .success-box {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1f3a2a 0%, #2a4a3a 100%);
  }
  :global([data-theme="dark"]) .success-box h4,
  :global([data-theme="dark"]) .success-box ol { color: #c8e6c9; }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    header h1 { font-size: 1.8em; }
    .subtitle { font-size: 1em; }
    .level-nav { flex-direction: column; }
    .level-nav .nav-btn { width: 100%; text-align: center; }
  }
</style>
